<p>The curriculum approach achieves <strong>50.0% on AIME 2024</strong> under diffusion decoding with B=4 inference, and <strong>48.3% with B=32 inference</strong> — better than the fixed B=4 baseline at large-block inference (42.5%), and far better than fixed B=32 training (20.0%). One model covers the full efficiency-quality Pareto frontier.</p>
</section>

<!-- ─── §05 RelaxedConfidence ──────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="s-relaxed" data-code="relaxed">
<div class="section-no">05 — RelaxedConfidence Decoding</div>
<h2>Conservative thresholds leave efficiency on the table</h2>
<p>Block diffusion uses a <em>confidence-threshold</em> decoding strategy: at each denoising step, a token is committed if its predicted confidence exceeds threshold τ (typically 0.95). Tokens below τ remain masked and get another denoising pass.</p>
<p>The problem: this threshold treats every token independently. In practice, <strong>contiguous spans of tokens</strong> reach implicit stability together — a sequence like "the answer is 42" either stabilizes as a unit or not. The 0.95 threshold is overly conservative for the middle tokens in such a span.</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">RelaxedConfidence — spatial support lowers the per-token threshold</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">hover over a token to see its effective threshold</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <canvas id="canvas-relaxed" style="width:100%;height:220px;display:block;border-radius:6px;cursor:crosshair"></canvas>
    <div id="relaxed-info" style="font-size:.73rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:.75rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);text-align:center">hover over a token above</div>
  </div>
</div>

<p>RelaxedConfidence introduces a <strong>position-specific threshold</strong> τᵢ that depends on how many <em>reliable neighbors</em> surround position i. Tokens flanked by already-decoded or high-confidence neighbors get a lower effective threshold (down to τ_min), while isolated tokens still need to pass the full τ=0.95 bar.</p>

<div class="math-block">
<div class="math-label">RelaxedConfidence threshold formula</div>
Sᵢ = (Σ<sub>j∈Nr(i)∩R</sub> wᵢⱼ) / (Σ<sub>j∈Nr(i)</sub> wᵢⱼ)   <span class="math-comment">← spatial support score</span>
<br>
τᵢ = τ − (τ − τ_min) · Sᵢ   <span class="math-comment">← position-specific threshold</span>
<br><br>
Sᵢ=0 (isolated): τᵢ = τ = 0.95   <span class="math-comment">← full threshold</span>
Sᵢ=1 (well-supported): τᵢ = τ_min   <span class="math-comment">← relaxed threshold</span>
</div>

<p>This yields substantial TPF gains with minimal accuracy cost. During the <strong>answering phase</strong> — where outputs are structured and lexically constrained — RelaxedConfidence raises TPF from ~2.4 to ~3.6 on AIME 2025 (+50%) and from ~3.9 to ~6.2 on LiveCodeBench (+59%).</p>
</section>

